hi there Steve Kaufman and today again I  want to talk about communicating in  language learning it's so important we  communicate when we speak obviously but  we also communicate when we listen and  read and the other day on our forum at  link someone said that they had been  working at link and listening and  reading and they felt as if they weren't  making any progress they didn't feel  that they understood any better than  three months earlier they had done a 90  day challenge at length I'm going to ask  that person are you listening to and are  you reading things that you're really  interested in in other words is this  compelling content this is something  that stephen krashen refers to all the  time compelling content if what you are  reading and listening to is a great  interest to you and I might add if  you're listening to something where you  enjoy the voice and the subject is of  interest and possibly the subject is  familiar to you I don't see how you  can't understand more and more if on the  other hand you're listening to something  that's not interesting and you're  listening over and over again yes you  are going to basically stop progressing  because the brain requires things that  are stimulating even in terms of  learning content it has to be  stimulating in some way and I have made  reference in previous videos to this  interleaving that it's a good idea  sometimes to leave some something that  you're working on go and do something  else study some other subject and then  come back to it and all of this  refreshes the brain and the brain learns  better rather than trying to sort of  learn a block of something or force  yourself to learn something that's not  very interesting to you so communicating  is is the best way to learn  communication whether it be listening  and reading which I consider to be  communicating or speaking this is the  key to learning but it has to be  compelling it has to be you know of  interest and the more compelling the  nicer the voice in your ears the more  you are attracted to the subject  better you're going to learn so remember  stephen krashen with his compelling  content it has to be compelling if it's  very compelling it can be very difficult  for you but you'll work your way through  it so communicating but meaningful  compelling communication thanks for  listening
 

